@0    = ~...And your point is?~
@1    = ~You do not even understand what it is you are getting into. She is a Bhaalspawn, a creature not of your knowledge. She is...she...~
@2    = ~Yeah, and she's also a woman who maybe needs a friend - rather than some doomsayer talking her ear off about how she's going to die soon.~
@3    = ~(sigh)~
@4    = ~You...care for her, then.~
@5    = ~Sure I do. She's great. I mean, I don't know her that well, but it's not like that matters, is it?~
@6    = ~Seldarine, why must I deal with this? This, on top of everything else?~
@7    = ~Okay, I've got something to talk to you about.~
@8    = ~It's Xan. I'm not - jealous, not really - but he's been breathing down your neck all the time, lately, making eyes. Is there something I should know?~
@9    = ~I prefer spending time with you, not Xan.~
@10   = ~I like your company, Faren, but I consider us no more than friends.~
@11   = ~In that case, I won't worry over it. Thanks for clearing that up, <CHARNAME>.~
@12   = ~Ah. I see. Well, if you prefer that kind of thing, go for it, I guess.~
@13   = ~I wonder, sometimes, why you continue your travels after your companions perished.~
@14   = ~You're a ray of sunshine, aren't you? Feeling on top form?~
@15   = ~Surely you recognised your friends' deaths as a hint from the fates that your path was not to be. Why choose to prolong the suffering?~
@16   = ~Oh, I hung around moping a bit, believe me, but honestly? I got bored.~
@17   = ~Boredom is no reason to risk your neck at <CHARNAME>'s side.~
@18   = ~Good a reason as any.~
@19   = ~It never ceases to amaze me how many unfortunate souls we gather as compatriots on our journey. I wonder how many will survive.~
@20   = ~You do realise I'm right here, right?~
@21   = ~What of it?~
@22   = ~Kind of rude to talk about me dying like I'm not here.~
@23   = ~Is it? Or perhaps I simply recognise the danger in our surroundings.~
@24   = ~Yeah, I get that. Just wondering when you'll realise how much good stuff there is in the world.~
@25   = ~Oh, believe me, I am aware of such things. I merely know I will not live to sample most of them.~
@26   = ~Every day is another step towards our destruction. I thought it would end with Sarevok. At least he would have killed us quickly. But Irenicus and his experiments...I shudder to imagine what he has planned for us.~
@27   = ~Well, so long as you getting into a tizz helps you remember those spells of yours, I'm happy.~
@28   = ~Hey, check that out! That cloud looks like a cat!~
@29   = ~It looks like a dog. A dog, with open jaws about to eat a foolish rat.~
@30   = ~That's a ball of wool, not a rat. Well, I guess if you squint...~
@31   = ~Squint all you wish. At least when our enemies are upon us they will dispatch us quickly, while you are so distracted.~
@32   = ~It shall never cease to amaze me how <CHARNAME>'s erstwhile companions convince themselves they ought to live and die at <PRO_HISHER> word.~
@33   = ~Pot calling the kettle black, Xan. You've spent more time with <PRO_HIMHER> than me, haven't you? How long was it - months?~
@34   = ~Hey! I'm not having Xan muscling in on my turf. I'm the childhood friend 'round here, not him!~
@35   = ~It does sometimes feel longer than it has been, certainly. Travelling with <CHARNAME> is never peaceful, but there are always...things going on.~
@36   = ~Minsc needs no convincing! <CHARNAME> and Minsc and Boo are compatriots!~
@37   = ~As I recall, Minsc, you did not know that word until yesterday.~
@38   = ~So if you're so scared, why'd you hang around with all this death and danger?~
@39   = ~Seldarine help me, but I care for <CHARNAME>.~
@40   = ~There is no fear, if you have nothing to lose.~
